# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows checkouts.
#
# There are none in the tree right now. The rule stays because the failure it
# prevents is invisible: a .sh shipped in a ConfigMap and read by bash inside a
# Linux container dies on CRLF with "set: pipefail: invalid option name", and
# the carriage return shows up in no editor and in no `kubectl get cm -o yaml`.
*.sh text eol=lf
